@title Heat: the cabinet follows the chosen enclosure (small synthetic enclosure)
@area Heat
@sizes 1366x768
# Fixture qa/fixtures/cabinet-heat-spec-small.novo (make_heat_spec_fixtures.py): the example cabinet with an `encl.` record, synthetic catalogue enclosure 1000x1400x300 mm. Compare with 9501 (1400x1800x500): same devices and plate, only the record differs, so the heat result must differ. The enclosure line and the estimate sentence sit behind the Temperature panel's "?" (second picture). The visible tag "(estimate)" stays on screen (first picture).
open qa/fixtures/cabinet-heat-spec-small.novo
wait 20
click_text Cabinet #1
wait 20
key ctrl+k
wait 3
text Simulate heat of the cabinet
wait 4
key Enter
wait_s 60
expect "· it "
expect "(estimate)"
shot 01-small-spec
check_blank 01-small-spec
check_layout
# The "?" is painted in the title bar, not a widget: click it by position (1366x768: 1293,201; the 1920x1080 twin scenario clicks 1847,201).
click 1293 201
wait 8
expect "Estimate from catalogue"
shot 02-help-open
